OL,3,GNEWSATown crier of 40 years dies after
OL,4,Aroyal honour
OL,5,
OL,6,FA town crier who served for 40 years
OL,7,Fhas died at the age of 82 shortly after
OL,8,Freceiving the British Empire Medal.
OL,10,FTrevor Heeks was appointed town crier
OL,11,Fof Trowbridge, Wiltshire, after a
OL,12,Fpublic contest in 1986 and went on to
OL,13,Fwin more than 160 competitions locally,
OL,14,Fregionally, nationally and even a world
OL,15,Fchampionship.
OL,17,FHe received the honour officially
OL,18,Fearlier in October while at the Royal
OL,19,FUnited Hospital, in Bath, from Lord
OL,20,FLieutenant of Wiltshire, Dame Sarah
OL,21,FTroughton, and was also recognised for
OL,22,Fhis work with twinning.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
